              {
                "old_text": "# Helpers\n\nUtilities.\n",
                "new_text": "# Helpers\n\nUtilities for working with numbers and labels.\n\n## numbers.total(values)\n\nSums numeric values in the iterable `values`, ignoring `None`. Zero and negative numbers are kept.\nAn empty iterable or an iterable containing only `None` returns `0`.\n\nExamples:\n\n```python\nfrom numbers import total\n\ntotal([2, None, -1, 0])  # 1\ntotal([None])             # 0\ntotal([])                 # 0\n```\n\n## labels.normalize(value)\n\nNormalizes a string label by trimming leading and trailing whitespace, converting to lowercase,\nand preserving internal spaces.\n\nExamples:\n\n```python\nfrom labels import normalize\n\nnormalize(' A B ')  # 'a b'\nnormalize('  ')     # ''\n```\n"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
